{"name":"Vampire Hunter","hex":"#610507","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vampire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mythological creature (usually humanoid and undead) said to feed on the blood or life energy of the living. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A person with habits traditionally ascribed to (literal) vampires, such as heliophobia, being a night owl, having pale skin, and so on."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To drain of energy or resources."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vampire"},{"term":"hunter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who hunts game for sport or for food; a huntsman or huntswoman.","A dog used in hunting; a hunting dog."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hunter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vampire hunter","blocks":[{"text":"A vampire hunter or vampire slayer is a fictional occupation in folklore and fiction which specializes in finding vampires, and sometimes other mythical creatures. A vampire hunter is usually described as having extensive knowledge of vampires and other monstrous or undead creatures, including their powers and weaknesses, and uses this knowledge to effectively combat them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Vampire_killing_kit%2C_Royal_Armouries.jpg/330px-Vampire_killing_kit%2C_Royal_Armouries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire_hunter","wikidata":"Q1058307"},{"title":"Vampire","blocks":[{"text":"A vampire is a mythical creature with a human-like appearance that subsists by feeding on the vital essence of humans. In European folklore, vampires are undead humanoid creatures that visit loved ones and cause mischief or deaths in the neighbourhoods they inhabited while they were alive. They wear shrouds and are often described as bloated and of ruddy or dark countenance, contrasting with the modern gaunt, pale vampire which dates from the early 19th century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Philip_Burne-Jones_-_The_Vampire.jpg/330px-Philip_Burne-Jones_-_The_Vampire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire","wikidata":"Q46721"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Vampire_killing_kit%2C_Royal_Armouries.jpg/500px-Vampire_killing_kit%2C_Royal_Armouries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Vampire_killing_kit%2C_Royal_Armouries.jpg/1280px-Vampire_killing_kit%2C_Royal_Armouries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Vampire_killing_kit%2C_Royal_Armouries.jpg/500px-Vampire_killing_kit%2C_Royal_Armouries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"in folklore and fiction, vampire hunters used special equipment to kill vampires. This inspired the creation and sale of vampire killing kits. This kit, which includes wooden stakes, a mallet, a crucifix, and a pistol, is a modern assembly on display at the Royal Armouries.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVampire_killing_kit%2C_Royal_Armouries.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Philip_Burne-Jones_-_The_Vampire.jpg/500px-Philip_Burne-Jones_-_The_Vampire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Philip_Burne-Jones_-_The_Vampire.jpg/500px-Philip_Burne-Jones_-_The_Vampire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Vampire, by Philip Burne-Jones, 1897","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhilip_Burne-Jones_-_The_Vampire.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.w